## Flags the release's VM starts with: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## The release sets -mode, -name, -sname, and -setcookie from its environment.

## The segment allocator keeps no freed segment in its cache, so a segment a
## process heap or a binary frees goes back to the system at once and the
## resident size follows what the VM holds. A full sweep of a large heap
## allocates the new heap and frees the old one, and with the default cache of
## 10 segments of any size the freed heaps stay resident: replayed against
## production's stored responses on 2026-11-08, a start reached 1,370 MiB
## resident with at most 581 MB allocated, past the container's 1,536 MB limit
## once the tile build ran beside it, and 565 MiB with no cache (GOB-275).
## https://www.erlang.org/doc/apps/erts/erts_alloc.html#flags-for-configuration-of-mseg_alloc — checked 2026-11-08
+MMmcs 0
